+    "body": "An authored mutation error currently appears as a resumable internal fault. This change publishes nonresumable `MUTATION_ERROR` failures with the node, operation index/kind and a bounded author diagnostic. Authored Exit evaluation errors use `EXPRESSION_ERROR`. Unexpected failures keep their recovery behavior while newly published run records and events exclude private exception messages, paths and stacks; correlated server logs retain the diagnostic.\n\nThe handling preserves atomic mutations, repair and raw-fallback outcomes, cancellation/deadline precedence, script classification, inference recording order, and subloop recovery metadata. Historical rows and events are unchanged. ADR-0080, the numbered documentation, CHANGELOG and generated API types describe the new-record boundary.\n\nCloses #381. Incorporates the criteria consolidated from #414.\n\nValidation:\n\n- Focused candidate checks: 1,070 tests; final isolated domain coverage: 460 tests, 98.74% lines / 95.98% branches; final engine coverage: 1,812 tests, 96.94% lines / 91.22% branches. Types, lint, schema generation, templates, licences, documentation and contrast checks are recorded in the [implementation evidence](https://github.com/Jacob-J-Thomas/GraphGoblin/blob/5082bc176e92cf3518abb630a5afc0a59c444815/docs/qa/2026-11-15-runtime-failure-implementation/README.md).\n- Independent candidate QA: 18 functional and 13 internal cases on the frozen source/build, with explicit zero-exit receipts and owned-resource cleanup. This includes compiled REST/stdio MCP, real SQLite, the served Edge inspector, controlled fault ports and two native Node script controls. [Candidate evidence](https://github.com/Jacob-J-Thomas/GraphGoblin/blob/5082bc176e92cf3518abb630a5afc0a59c444815/docs/qa/2026-11-15-runtime-failure-candidate/README.md)\n- The original full local `pnpm check` failed during coverage. The packet preserves its complete outputs, later isolated results and unresolved causes in unrelated Windows suites; it does not claim a green full local run. Current publication-head CI remains a separate required gate.\n- The [unchanged-main baseline](https://github.com/Jacob-J-Thomas/GraphGoblin/blob/5082bc176e92cf3518abb630a5afc0a59c444815/docs/qa/2026-11-15-runtime-failure-baseline/README.md) preserves the reproduced behavior and original fixture/supervisor failures, including the missing internal baseline harness exit value.\n\nCurrent publication head: `693ea3c9d05359f6ebee8822dd566c99c3e4973c`, tree `7e611f71ac8b3693d574b8f08869d68fed19af4b`, against main `f91bd69b79dc417a2997ddb9c7670cb33df7597c`. [CI run 43745479496](https://github.com/Jacob-J-Thomas/GraphGoblin/actions/runs/43745479496) is now successful on this exact revision. Attempt 1 passed Browser (481 tests and one expected live-provider skip), Windows launcher (14 tests) and Template image. Its Gates job was cancelled at the configured 30-minute job limit after ten coverage groups, with later checks skipped. The original failure and partial artifact are retained. Exactly one unchanged-head [Gates-only retry](https://github.com/Jacob-J-Thomas/GraphGoblin/actions/runs/43745479496/job/132918799467) passed all 32 steps and all 13 coverage groups: 9,605 tests passed / 41 skipped, with every package above 90% lines and branches. Licences, generated docs, contrast and the configured dependency audit passed. The successful Browser/Windows/Template outcomes are carried forward from their original executions; they did not rerun. No assertions, thresholds, time limits or workflow inputs changed. The exact tested synthetic merge is `955dccf755f5f34387f990ff47fa49c7bbf45f55`, with target/head parents and the same publication tree. The earlier failed 5082 run and green 656a run are retained with their exact identities and limitations in the [CI packet](https://github.com/Jacob-J-Thomas/GraphGoblin/blob/693ea3c9d05359f6ebee8822dd566c99c3e4973c/docs/qa/2026-11-15-runtime-failure-ci/README.md); neither substitutes for this head's gates.\n\nClaude Opus 5.5 xhigh completed formal scan 1 with CHANGES REQUIRED for documentation only; it found no product or test blocker. GPT-6 Luna xhigh corrected the three affected documents, and separate GPT-6.1 Sol xhigh factual QA passed. F1 now accurately describes safe public diagnostics, correlated private logs and the named remaining authored evaluation boundaries; FU2 adds the current MUTATION_ERROR recovery instruction. Product, test and build inputs remain unchanged from source `615d50bc358d73bc55ad0591f4f625f1a46cb671`. Scoped formatting and diff checks passed. [Full review and dispositions](https://github.com/Jacob-J-Thomas/GraphGoblin/pull/485#issuecomment-6898705327) · [Review and correction evidence](https://github.com/Jacob-J-Thomas/GraphGoblin/blob/693ea3c9d05359f6ebee8822dd566c99c3e4973c/docs/qa/2026-11-15-runtime-failure-review/README.md)\n\nBroader authored-error classification is parked in #486 outside this batch. Fresh independent GPT-6 Astra max scan 2 is now running against this exact head and target, after root verified the complete current CI and coverage archive. It must independently verify F1 and the whole effective change; no final audit verdict has been issued. The shared three-scan cap remains intact. This draft is not a merge, issue-completion or owner-acceptance claim.\n\nThe evidence-only publication also records the already merged PR #484's [CI](https://github.com/Jacob-J-Thomas/GraphGoblin/blob/5082bc176e92cf3518abb630a5afc0a59c444815/docs/qa/2026-11-15-poll-dedupe-current-ci/README.md) and [completion](https://github.com/Jacob-J-Thomas/GraphGoblin/blob/5082bc176e92cf3518abb630a5afc0a59c444815/docs/qa/2026-11-15-poll-dedupe-completion/README.md). The delivery register keeps subsequent #410, #419 and launcher work separate.\n",
