+    "body": "An authored mutation error currently appears as a resumable internal fault. This change publishes nonresumable `MUTATION_ERROR` failures with the node, operation index/kind and a bounded author diagnostic. Authored Exit evaluation errors use `EXPRESSION_ERROR`. Unexpected failures keep their recovery behavior while newly published run records and events exclude private exception messages, paths and stacks; correlated server logs retain the diagnostic.\n\nThe handling preserves atomic mutations, repair and raw-fallback outcomes, cancellation/deadline precedence, script classification, inference recording order, and subloop recovery metadata. Historical rows and events are unchanged. ADR-0080, the numbered documentation, CHANGELOG and generated API types describe the new-record boundary.\n\nCloses #381. Incorporates the criteria consolidated from #414.\n\nValidation:\n\n- Focused candidate checks: 1,070 tests; final isolated domain coverage: 460 tests, 98.74% lines / 95.98% branches; final engine coverage: 1,812 tests, 96.94% lines / 91.22% branches. Types, lint, schema generation, templates, licences, documentation and contrast checks are recorded in the [implementation evidence](https://github.com/Jacob-J-Thomas/GraphGoblin/blob/5082bc176e92cf3518abb630a5afc0a59c444815/docs/qa/2026-11-15-runtime-failure-implementation/README.md).\n- Independent candidate QA: 18 functional and 13 internal cases on the frozen source/build, with explicit zero-exit receipts and owned-resource cleanup. This includes compiled REST/stdio MCP, real SQLite, the served Edge inspector, controlled fault ports and two native Node script controls. [Candidate evidence](https://github.com/Jacob-J-Thomas/GraphGoblin/blob/5082bc176e92cf3518abb630a5afc0a59c444815/docs/qa/2026-11-15-runtime-failure-candidate/README.md)\n- The original full local `pnpm check` failed during coverage. The packet preserves its complete outputs, later isolated results and unresolved causes in unrelated Windows suites; it does not claim a green full local run. Current publication-head CI remains a separate required gate.\n- The [unchanged-main baseline](https://github.com/Jacob-J-Thomas/GraphGoblin/blob/5082bc176e92cf3518abb630a5afc0a59c444815/docs/qa/2026-11-15-runtime-failure-baseline/README.md) preserves the reproduced behavior and original fixture/supervisor failures, including the missing internal baseline harness exit value.\n\nCurrent publication head: `656a73214c5d59a25c22a4abf2d8b3bf17976959`, against main `f91bd69b79dc417a2997ddb9c7670cb33df7597c`. The first [CI run 43735208367](https://github.com/Jacob-J-Thomas/GraphGoblin/actions/runs/43735208367) passed Browser, Windows launcher and Template image, but Gates failed formatting on six raw inspector HTML captures; all subsequent gates, including coverage, were skipped. The correction only excludes those capture paths from formatting, preserving all six hashes and the unchanged product/test/build inputs. Full local `pnpm.cmd format:check` passed. Fresh [current-head CI 43737977820](https://github.com/Jacob-J-Thomas/GraphGoblin/actions/runs/43737977820), attempt 1, passed all four jobs at synthetic merge `7c8cf9f2b8b099351a9ac138cab43d86ec5ad23f` (the exact target and head, tree `d6c3dc2f3ebf265133fc3761c775ed37b2077388`). Coverage recorded 9,605 passes and 41 skips across 13 packages, all above the required line/branch floors; Browser passed 481 with one declared live-provider skip and zero retries; Windows passed 14/14; Template image loaded all four installed templates. The downloaded coverage archive matches GitHub's SHA-256. Windows produced no downloadable artifact. Optional strict routing bounds were off. Claude Opus 5.5 xhigh formal scan 1 is in progress; fresh independent Astra max sign-off remains required within the shared three-scan cap.\n\nGPT-6.1 Sol xhigh implemented this slice. Separate Sol xhigh agents performed behavior QA. Claude Opus 5.5 xhigh adversarial review and fresh GPT-6 Astra max exact-head/target sign-off follow green current-head CI, under the shared three-scan cap. This draft is not a merge or owner-acceptance claim.\n\nThe evidence-only publication also records the already merged PR #484's [CI](https://github.com/Jacob-J-Thomas/GraphGoblin/blob/5082bc176e92cf3518abb630a5afc0a59c444815/docs/qa/2026-11-15-poll-dedupe-current-ci/README.md) and [completion](https://github.com/Jacob-J-Thomas/GraphGoblin/blob/5082bc176e92cf3518abb630a5afc0a59c444815/docs/qa/2026-11-15-poll-dedupe-completion/README.md). The delivery register keeps subsequent #410, #419 and launcher work separate.\n",
