+# #410 second native baseline
+
+All W1–W4 baseline assertions completed. W1 reproduced stale wait after live child failure. W2 reproduced stale wait when recovery consumed an already-committed failure event. W3 preserved active waits, success, cancellation and authored-exit behavior. W4 preserved the finalized historical parent and child. Root accepted this baseline for implementation. [Acceptance](C:/Users/98jak/graphgoblin-qa/2026-11-13-aidlc-batch/runtime-410-baseline-acceptance.json) · [Harness summary](C:/Users/98jak/graphgoblin-qa/2026-11-13-aidlc-batch/runtime-410-native-preparation/evidence-baseline-review-02/summary.json)
+
+## Execution and binding
+
+The runner used actual main `154401c7b47c1e56b62a6daec50e2a3145ea967d`, tree `7e611f71ac8b3693d574b8f08869d68fed19af4b` and the same successful build as attempt 01. Opening and closing bindings agreed for 28,329 source files, the index, 1,231 output files under 13 roots, Node v22.23.4, 17 selected dependency files and 22 workspace links. Six named runtime entry hashes matched the build output map. [Admission](C:/Users/98jak/graphgoblin-qa/2026-11-13-aidlc-batch/runtime-410-native-baseline-admission-02.json) · [Build binding](C:/Users/98jak/graphgoblin-qa/2026-11-13-aidlc-batch/runtime-410-build-baseline-review-01/build-binding.json) · [Launcher preflight](C:/Users/98jak/graphgoblin-qa/2026-11-13-aidlc-batch/runtime-410-launch-execution-baseline-review-02/preflight.json)
+
+Supervisor PID 55756 exited 0 at 2026-11-15T20:02:22.2983484Z with no deadline. PowerShell wrapper PID 52476 separately exited 0 in command completion chunk `298446`. The wrapper wrote raw child exit before its derived `matrix-finished-for-review` receipt. Both transcripts were empty. The harness reported `assertions-met` with no new first-failure receipt. [Launch identity](C:/Users/98jak/graphgoblin-qa/2026-11-13-aidlc-batch/runtime-410-launch-execution-baseline-review-02/launch.json) · [OS exit](C:/Users/98jak/graphgoblin-qa/2026-11-13-aidlc-batch/runtime-410-launch-execution-baseline-review-02/child-exit.json) · [Closing receipt](C:/Users/98jak/graphgoblin-qa/2026-11-13-aidlc-batch/runtime-410-launch-execution-baseline-review-02/launch-result.json)
+
+## W1 and W3 on the ordinary compiled gateway
+
+W1 parent `01M7GCTTXCMV33QH3MVHKBNC4G` and child `01M7GCTV0C71AVADY59KRSX5W0` parked on real child and input waits. The fixture answered the observed input wait. Bound Node PID 35624, a child of the gateway, wrote one marker in the owned store and exited 7. The finalized pair retained `SCRIPT_EXIT_CODE`, completed visit and dispatch identity, and stderr `qa410-local-exit7`. The parent history kept child park seq 7, wake seq 8 naming child terminal seq 14, child completion seq 10 and the sole `run.failed` seq 11. Its SQL wait matched the earlier park bytes. REST detail and two-page listing, and compiled stdio MCP detail and two-page listing exposed the same stale wait ID ending in `:5`. Both public replays agreed with SQLite.
+
+The second parked pair's rows and events stayed byte-identical while other runs completed. The success pair cleared both waits and the parent completed its subloop and entered its exit once. Reusing the consumed child wait returned HTTP 409 `WAIT_MISMATCH` and the fixture compared the unchanged child row and events. The authored failure exit finalized through `run.finished` with outcome `failure`, a SQL NULL wait and no typed failure. Cancellation finalized both previously parked runs with SQL NULL waits. Root's first offline comparison included the surrounding list pages and failed. Its corrected comparison targeted the raw parent and child rows and events, which matched. No native rerun followed.
+
+## W2 event-first interruption and ordinary restart
+
+The pre-delegate gate held parent `01M7GCV3P3TFNV59ETMDXNTFE2` in exact owned gateway PID 50840, Windows creation identity `134392465253392000`. The gate reported `delegateEntered: false`, failed change and no `waiting` member. The independent SQLite reader saw one committed `run.failed` seq 11 matching the gate, after child completion. The parent remained `running` with its original wait, checkpoint seq 7 and SQL NULL failure, finish and finalization. The child was finalized and bound Node PID 53332 had produced one exit-7 marker. The pre-interruption receipt last write was 2026-11-15T20:02:10.9597480Z. [Durable landing receipt](C:/Users/98jak/graphgoblin-qa/2026-11-13-aidlc-batch/runtime-410-native-preparation/evidence-baseline-review-02/W2-verified-before-interruption.json)
+
+Only the exact proven gated process handle was interrupted. Its exit and pipe close both reported `SIGKILL` and its former listener refused TCP. The fixture saved DB, WAL and SHM hashes and identities, including a 1,351,392-byte WAL, before restart. Ordinary PID 31520 reopened the same store with a new Windows creation identity. The fixture checked the database device and file ID. Recovery finalized the parent and advanced its checkpoint to seq 11. The exact same failure event, parent journal and child row/events remained, and the script marker did too. The old wait bytes remained in SQL and in REST and MCP detail and list responses. The W2 gate was a composed repository port. The restart used ordinary compiled startup. [Post-crash receipt](C:/Users/98jak/graphgoblin-qa/2026-11-13-aidlc-batch/runtime-410-native-preparation/evidence-baseline-review-02/W2-post-crash-before-reopen.json) · [Restart readback](C:/Users/98jak/graphgoblin-qa/2026-11-13-aidlc-batch/runtime-410-native-preparation/evidence-baseline-review-02/summary.json)
+
+## W4 and seed provenance
+
+After W1/W3 shutdown, the helper copied the complete DB/WAL/SHM bundle from attempt 02. Every input hash matched its staging copy. Bound Node helper PID 52644 checkpointed only the copy. `wal_checkpoint(TRUNCATE)` returned busy 0, log 0 and checkpointed 0, and journal mode returned `delete`. It exited and closed both output pipes with code 0. Its read-only queries independently reproduced the exact captured W1 parent and child rows and ordered event values. Source bundle hashes still matched before ordinary scratch cleanup. Checkpointing changed the SQLite file hash.
+
+The private transfer seed is one regular 552,960-byte database with SHA-256 `07147c5fc50b1ac4f9ef2c2629d89396a7a3ed60ce4e7631bb7743a12cd8f7a5` and no sidecars. A verified separate copy opened in the W4 ordinary gateway. Both finalized W1 raw rows and their exact event values survived restart, including the stale parent wait. There was no script rerun. The closed seed remains bound to parent `01M7GCTTXCMV33QH3MVHKBNC4G` and this baseline summary. The cause of the first attempt's WAL persistence remains unknown. [Derivation and W4 readback](C:/Users/98jak/graphgoblin-qa/2026-11-13-aidlc-batch/runtime-410-native-preparation/evidence-baseline-review-02/summary.json) · [Correction preparation](C:/Users/98jak/graphgoblin-qa/2026-11-13-aidlc-batch/runtime-410-native-seed-correction-preparation/preparation.json)
+
