+# #410 fixture preflight after #381
+
+Static comparison against runtime checkout `693ea3c9d05359f6ebee8822dd566c99c3e4973c`, which contains #381 production commit `615d50bc358d73bc55ad0591f4f625f1a46cb671`. The existing W1–W4 fixture and corrected supervisor match the checked source seams. I found no fixture admission correction for #381.
+
+- **W1 script and parent failure.** The fixture passes the bound Node executable, separate `-e` arguments, and the disposable store as cwd. The native adapter still passes these through to `spawn` and inherits the gateway environment, so the marker's cwd/`GG_DATA_DIR` test and exit-7 inputs still match. The script handler reports the completed dispatch as `SCRIPT_EXIT_CODE` with the recorded visit and dispatch, `exitCode: 7`, and captured streams. The subloop handler carries the same code and script evidence forward with `childRunId`, `childNodeId`, and `childDetails`. The #381 child-details renderer leaves this script result shape intact. The `RunErrorCodeSchema` adds `MUTATION_ERROR` and leaves this fixture's code and fields available. [Fixture](C:/Users/98jak/graphgoblin-qa/2026-11-13-aidlc-batch/runtime-410-native-preparation/run.mjs:195) · [Native process adapter](C:/Users/98jak/.codex/worktrees/gg-20261115-runtime/GraphGoblin/packages/infrastructure/src/process/scripts.ts:119) · [Script handler](C:/Users/98jak/.codex/worktrees/gg-20261115-runtime/GraphGoblin/packages/engine/src/handlers/script.ts:123) · [Subloop handler](C:/Users/98jak/.codex/worktrees/gg-20261115-runtime/GraphGoblin/packages/engine/src/handlers/subloop.ts:260) · [Failure renderer](C:/Users/98jak/.codex/worktrees/gg-20261115-runtime/GraphGoblin/packages/engine/src/failure-publication.ts:87) · [Failure schema](C:/Users/98jak/.codex/worktrees/gg-20261115-runtime/GraphGoblin/packages/contracts/src/run.ts:159)
+- **W2 journal/projection boundary.** The composed gateway still intercepts the shared `owner.ports.runs.transition` for the exact parent's failed status before the SQLite delegate. `failRun` appends terminal history before that call and its change object still has no `waiting` member at this head. The SQLite transition changes only supplied fields. An independent reader can therefore test the existing W2 oracle for a committed `run.failed` alongside the pre-transition active projection and original wait. On normal startup the run manager queues the active row and `completeFromLog` recognizes the stored `run.failed` before handler execution. That branch uses the stored failure and finalizes the projection, without another terminal event or script dispatch. [Composition gate](C:/Users/98jak/graphgoblin-qa/2026-11-13-aidlc-batch/runtime-410-native-preparation/gateway.mjs:37) · [API container](C:/Users/98jak/.codex/worktrees/gg-20261115-runtime/GraphGoblin/apps/api/src/container.ts:350) · [Failure publication](C:/Users/98jak/.codex/worktrees/gg-20261115-runtime/GraphGoblin/packages/engine/src/run-manager.ts:3039) · [SQLite transition](C:/Users/98jak/.codex/worktrees/gg-20261115-runtime/GraphGoblin/packages/infrastructure/src/sqlite/runs.ts:22) · [Recovery dispatch](C:/Users/98jak/.codex/worktrees/gg-20261115-runtime/GraphGoblin/packages/engine/src/run-manager.ts:2342) · [Journal completion](C:/Users/98jak/.codex/worktrees/gg-20261115-runtime/GraphGoblin/packages/engine/src/run-manager.ts:2824)
+- **W3 controls and readback interfaces.** The authored `returns: 'none'` exit still produces normal terminal history for both outcomes, and those projections and cancellation explicitly clear the wait. The strict wait-ID input route and HTTP 409 `WAIT_MISMATCH` remain available. REST detail, lists and event replay and the MCP stdio `get_run`, `list_runs`, and `read_run_events` tools still expose the fixture's full or summarized fields. MCP summaries retain the wait and typed script failure fields when present. SQLite still stores the same `waiting`, `failure`, event cursor and snapshot fields used by raw readback. [Controls](C:/Users/98jak/graphgoblin-qa/2026-11-13-aidlc-batch/runtime-410-native-preparation/run.mjs:445) · [Exit handler](C:/Users/98jak/.codex/worktrees/gg-20261115-runtime/GraphGoblin/packages/engine/src/handlers/exit.ts:8) · [Terminal projection](C:/Users/98jak/.codex/worktrees/gg-20261115-runtime/GraphGoblin/packages/engine/src/run-manager.ts:2862) · [Cancellation](C:/Users/98jak/.codex/worktrees/gg-20261115-runtime/GraphGoblin/packages/engine/src/run-manager.ts:3077) · [REST routes](C:/Users/98jak/.codex/worktrees/gg-20261115-runtime/GraphGoblin/apps/api/src/routes/runs.ts:131) · [Input route](C:/Users/98jak/.codex/worktrees/gg-20261115-runtime/GraphGoblin/apps/api/src/routes/runs.ts:418) · [HTTP error map](C:/Users/98jak/.codex/worktrees/gg-20261115-runtime/GraphGoblin/apps/api/src/plugins/errors.ts:65) · [MCP tools](C:/Users/98jak/.codex/worktrees/gg-20261115-runtime/GraphGoblin/apps/mcp/src/tools.ts:250) · [MCP summaries](C:/Users/98jak/.codex/worktrees/gg-20261115-runtime/GraphGoblin/apps/mcp/src/describe.ts:127) · [SQLite schema](C:/Users/98jak/.codex/worktrees/gg-20261115-runtime/GraphGoblin/packages/infrastructure/src/sqlite/schema.ts:83)
+- **W4 existing history.** The fixture seeds from the fully finalized W1 parent and child captured on the eventual baseline. SQLite recovery selection excludes finalized terminal rows. #381's child-details handling runs when forming a new parent failure and the current row decoder still reads stored failure JSON. The expected raw-row and event byte preservation on W4 restart is compatible with those paths. The corrected supervisor reads the existing `W4.seed` parent/database identity and hash and the two W2 evidence filenames published by the fixture. [Historical fixture](C:/Users/98jak/graphgoblin-qa/2026-11-13-aidlc-batch/runtime-410-native-preparation/run.mjs:613) · [Recovery selection](C:/Users/98jak/.codex/worktrees/gg-20261115-runtime/GraphGoblin/packages/infrastructure/src/sqlite/runs.ts:213) · [Run row decoder](C:/Users/98jak/.codex/worktrees/gg-20261115-runtime/GraphGoblin/packages/infrastructure/src/sqlite/run-row.ts:18) · [Supervisor](C:/Users/98jak/graphgoblin-qa/2026-11-13-aidlc-batch/runtime-410-launch-preparation/launch.ps1:229)
+
+Read-only SHA-256 verification matched all five [native payloads](C:/Users/98jak/graphgoblin-qa/2026-11-13-aidlc-batch/runtime-410-native-preparation/SHA256SUMS.txt) and all six [corrected launch payloads](C:/Users/98jak/graphgoblin-qa/2026-11-13-aidlc-batch/runtime-410-launch-preparation/PREPARATION-SHA256SUMS). Native manifest `acd42fe76f48392598096d15833302792906eb95467c3124cbadb69b8d47296f`. Corrected launch manifest `ed4badf92566e77316966c38e45c271c290425db1084a1fb616f3e1934321ae0`.
+
+The actual #410 baseline remains pending #381 merge and fresh source, index, build and supervisor binding. The process marker, independent WAL landing observation, Windows process identity and interruption, stdio lifecycle, and restart behavior require the admitted native execution.
