index 00000000..abdd8909
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/qa/2026-11-15-terminal-wait-candidate/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,24 @@
+# Terminal-wait candidate evidence (#410)
+
+Root accepted the first admitted candidate native execution after independent QA passed W1-W4. The packet preserves the sealed QA report and inventory, raw candidate evidence, the bound build proof, launcher receipts and root readbacks. Source artifacts are copied byte-for-byte; the raw Markdown report is named `.md.txt` to preserve its sealed bytes. The [source-copy map](source-copy-map.json) records absolute batch root and source paths, sizes and hashes. The [packet checksum file](SHA256SUMS) covers every packet file except itself.
+
+## Source and bound build
+
+The candidate is commit `4e4501bd92953794bb733a746f7c24d1bcc2452a`, tree `8f19c61271418529ff96e8e204c18010ce088c5e`, based on `154401c7b47c1e56b62a6daec50e2a3145ea967d`. The exact [source acceptance receipt](../2026-11-15-terminal-wait-implementation/provenance/runtime-410-source-root-acceptance.json) is preserved in the sibling implementation packet.
+
+The forced Node 22.23.4 build completed 12 tasks with zero Turbo cache hits. Candidate source and output binding reported 28,329 source files and 1,231 output files across 13 roots. The 4,293,619-byte full build binding remains external at `C:\Users\98jak\graphgoblin-qa\2026-11-13-aidlc-batch\runtime-410-build-candidate-review-01\build-binding.json`, SHA-256 `cbf6bbd47aa7c556443e31afad40d39ea7425bc5b6b073c4754bfef393c3a38a`; this packet excludes that large file. The [candidate build receipt](candidate/build/build-receipt.json) and [build acceptance](provenance/runtime-410-candidate-build-root-acceptance.json) preserve the accepted binding.
+
+## Candidate results
+
+| Case                                   | Observed result                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                |
+| -------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
+| W1 live child failure                  | Parent and child finalized with one typed `SCRIPT_EXIT_CODE` failure. Parent `waiting` became SQL NULL and was omitted from REST/MCP detail and list responses; event history remained intact.                                                                                                                                                                 |
+| W2 failure committed before projection | The composed public repository-port gate held the failed parent projection after `run.failed` committed. QA interrupted that exact gateway worker; ordinary compiled gateway startup then reopened the same store, finalized the parent with SQL NULL and no public wait, and preserved the single terminal event and child state without rerunning the child. |
+| W3 controls                            | Other active waits and raw rows/events stayed unchanged. Success and cancellation cleared waits; authored failure retained its expected `run.finished` outcome. Reusing the consumed input wait returned 409 without mutating the child.                                                                                                                       |
+| W4 historical boundary                 | The already-finalized baseline parent and child rows/events remained unchanged, including the stale wait still returned publicly. No migration or stored-value rewrite is included.                                                                                                                                                                            |
+
+The QA supervisor and PowerShell wrapper both exited 0, the harness reported `assertions-met`, all 15 owned PID slots were absent at cleanup, the four tested ports refused connections, and candidate stores were empty. The [root candidate acceptance](provenance/runtime-410-candidate-root-acceptance.json), [offline readback](provenance/runtime-410-candidate-root-offline-readback.json), [offline verifier source](provenance/runtime-410-candidate-root-verify.mjs), [launcher result](candidate/launch/launch-result.json), [raw candidate summary](candidate/native-evidence/summary.json), and [independent QA report](qa/report.md.txt) retain the details.
+
+The independent report and its [inventory](qa/inventory.json) are byte-verified against the copied [QA seal manifest](qa/SHA256SUMS.txt). No SQLite database or seed bytes are copied. The accepted native baseline fixtures and private seed evidence remain in the [sibling baseline packet](../2026-11-15-terminal-wait-baseline/README.md).
+
+This packet makes no current-head CI, cross-family review, security-audit, merge, owner-acceptance, or issue-completion claim.
