+# #410 native candidate
+
+Root accepted the first admitted candidate execution after all four cases satisfied their checks. The failed parent clears its wait both live and after restart, with one typed failure and intact child history. Success, authored failure, live waiting and cancellation retain their baseline behavior. The previously finalized historical parent and child retain their original row and event values. [Candidate summary](C:/Users/98jak/graphgoblin-qa/2026-11-13-aidlc-batch/runtime-410-native-preparation/evidence-candidate-review-01/summary.json) · [Root acceptance](C:/Users/98jak/graphgoblin-qa/2026-11-13-aidlc-batch/runtime-410-candidate-root-acceptance.json) · [Root offline readback](C:/Users/98jak/graphgoblin-qa/2026-11-13-aidlc-batch/runtime-410-candidate-root-offline-readback.json) · [Accepted baseline](C:/Users/98jak/graphgoblin-qa/2026-11-13-aidlc-batch/runtime-410-native-baseline-review-02-report/report.md)
+
+## Bound build and actual exits
+
+The candidate was `4e4501bd92953794bb733a746f7c24d1bcc2452a` on actual main `154401c7b47c1e56b62a6daec50e2a3145ea967d`, tree `8f19c61271418529ff96e8e204c18010ce088c5e`. The forced candidate build ran from 2026-11-15T20:10:12.809Z to 2026-11-15T20:10:34.421Z, exited 0, and reported 12 successful tasks and zero Turbo cache hits. Its full 4,293,619-byte binding stays external at the linked path. Opening and closing verification matched 28,329 source files and the index, 1,231 outputs under 13 roots, Node v22.23.4, 17 selected dependency files and 22 workspace links. All six declared fixture runtime entries matched the bound output hashes. [Admission](C:/Users/98jak/graphgoblin-qa/2026-11-13-aidlc-batch/runtime-410-native-candidate-admission-01.json) · [Build exit](C:/Users/98jak/graphgoblin-qa/2026-11-13-aidlc-batch/runtime-410-build-candidate-review-01/build-exit.json) · [Build receipt](C:/Users/98jak/graphgoblin-qa/2026-11-13-aidlc-batch/runtime-410-build-candidate-review-01/build-receipt.json) · [Build log](C:/Users/98jak/graphgoblin-qa/2026-11-13-aidlc-batch/runtime-410-build-candidate-review-01/build.log) · [Full external build binding](C:/Users/98jak/graphgoblin-qa/2026-11-13-aidlc-batch/runtime-410-build-candidate-review-01/build-binding.json)
+
+Supervisor PID 47204 exited 0 at 2026-11-15T20:14:43.9063887Z with no deadline. PowerShell wrapper PID 22048 separately exited 0 in tool chunk `841033`. The launcher wrote the OS exit receipt before the derived `matrix-finished-for-review` result. The harness reported `assertions-met`. Both transcript files were empty, and the run produced no first-failure receipt. [OS exit](C:/Users/98jak/graphgoblin-qa/2026-11-13-aidlc-batch/runtime-410-launch-execution-candidate-review-01/child-exit.json) · [Launch identity](C:/Users/98jak/graphgoblin-qa/2026-11-13-aidlc-batch/runtime-410-launch-execution-candidate-review-01/launch.json) · [Closing verification](C:/Users/98jak/graphgoblin-qa/2026-11-13-aidlc-batch/runtime-410-launch-execution-candidate-review-01/launch-result.json)
+
+## W1 live failed parent
+
+The ordinary compiled gateway parked parent `01M7GDHGXPMCNVW7SVKT3B1QK6` on its child and child `01M7GDHH0MNXA74T7DTG2F6GT1` on input. The fixture answered the observed child wait. Bound Node script PID 53044 produced one marker in the disposable store and exited 7. The child and parent finalized with `SCRIPT_EXIT_CODE`, the completed script visit and dispatch identities, and captured stderr `qa410-local-exit7`. Parent history retained park seq 7, wake seq 8 naming child terminal seq 14, matching child completion seq 10, and one `run.failed` seq 11. The raw parent wait became SQL NULL. REST detail, two-page REST list, MCP `get_run` and two-page `list_runs` each omitted the field. REST and MCP event readbacks matched raw SQLite. The accepted baseline exposed the stale wait in the equivalent four surfaces.
+
+## W2 committed failure before failed projection
+
+Parent `01M7GDHQZNG73Q04C8MV3KYQR3` initially parked on its child. The exact owned gateway PID 52008, Windows creation `134392472670935730`, stalled at the composed pre-delegate repository gate. The held failed transition owned the `waiting` member. The independent SQLite reader already saw one committed and matching `run.failed` seq 11. The parent remained `running` with original wait bytes, snapshot seq 7 and SQL NULL failure, finish and finalization. The child had finalized and genuine script PID 45940 had written the sole exit-7 marker. The verified receipt preceded interruption of that exact process handle. Both exit and pipe close reported `SIGKILL`. Before reopening, the fixture measured DB/WAL/SHM identity and hashes, including the 1,351,392-byte WAL. [Durable landing](C:/Users/98jak/graphgoblin-qa/2026-11-13-aidlc-batch/runtime-410-native-preparation/evidence-candidate-review-01/W2-verified-before-interruption.json) · [Post-crash receipt](C:/Users/98jak/graphgoblin-qa/2026-11-13-aidlc-batch/runtime-410-native-preparation/evidence-candidate-review-01/W2-post-crash-before-reopen.json)
+
+Ordinary gateway PID 34208 reopened the same store with a new Windows creation identity and the same database device and file ID. The parent finalized, checkpointed seq 11, and exposed SQL NULL and no public wait in REST or MCP detail and list results. The parent journal and exact child row/events matched the captured landing values, with one unchanged terminal failure event. The script marker matched and the child did not rerun. The W2 crash worker is native with a composed repository gate. The recovery restart is ordinary compiled startup.
+
+## W3 controls and W4 historical boundary
+
+The second still-parked pair retained exact raw parent and child rows and events while the other live runs completed. The successful pair cleared both waits, completed the parent subloop once and entered its exit once. Reusing the consumed input wait returned 409 `WAIT_MISMATCH` and left the child's raw row and events unchanged. An authored failure cleared its wait and emitted `run.finished` with outcome `failure`. Ordinary API cancellation then finalized both parked runs and cleared their waits.
+
+W4 reopened an independently hash-verified copy of the accepted baseline02 standalone SQLite seed for parent `01M7GCTTXCMV33QH3MVHKBNC4G`. Candidate readback matched the baseline W1 and W4 raw parent and child rows and ordered events exactly, including the already-finalized parent's stale wait. REST and MCP still returned that historical wait. The closed 552,960-byte original seed retained SHA-256 `07147c5fc50b1ac4f9ef2c2629d89396a7a3ed60ce4e7631bb7743a12cd8f7a5` with no sidecars. Its use and preservation were verified without reopening the original for this report. [Seed acceptance](C:/Users/98jak/graphgoblin-qa/2026-11-13-aidlc-batch/runtime-410-baseline-acceptance.json) · [Inventory](C:/Users/98jak/graphgoblin-qa/2026-11-13-aidlc-batch/runtime-410-native-candidate-review-01-report/inventory.json)
+
+## Cleanup and evidence boundary
+
+At 2026-11-15T20:15:43.9194813Z, independent Windows readback found all 15 owned PID slots absent and no listeners on 53353, 53458, 53490 or 51237. All four refused direct TCP. The three candidate store directories and launcher process-temp were empty. The fixture reported zero remaining writers, MCP sessions and SQLite observers. All 13 files from incomplete baseline01 and all 11 files from accepted baseline02 still matched their sealed lengths and hashes. QA used ordinary compiled REST, stdio MCP and file SQLite with real local Node children. The composed W2 gate supplied the crash boundary. [Independent inventory](C:/Users/98jak/graphgoblin-qa/2026-11-13-aidlc-batch/runtime-410-native-candidate-review-01-report/inventory.json) · [First baseline failure and recovery provenance](C:/Users/98jak/graphgoblin-qa/2026-11-13-aidlc-batch/runtime-410-native-baseline-review-01-report/report.md)
+
